  "scenario_text": "# Experiment D (part 1) - resilience policies against an unresponsive dependency (RQ2 / H2).\n# inventory-a hangs from t = 5 s to t = 25 s of a 40 s measurement (15 s after the fault to observe recovery,\n# including the breaker's 5 s reset timeout); fallback OFF so each policy's own\n# effect is visible. Lower rate (10 req/s) and a high in-flight cap because \"none\" holds requests\n# for up to 10 s.\n#   none                 timeout = outer deadline = 10 s (bounded only by the outer deadline)\n#   timeout              800 ms per attempt, no retries\n#   timeout-retry        800 ms, 2 retries (bound T*(1+r) + backoff, capped by the 3 s outer deadline)\n#   timeout-retry-breaker  as above + circuit breaker (5 consecutive failures, 5 s reset timeout)\nid: D_policies_hang\ntitle: \"D1 - Policies vs an unresponsive dependency\"\nhypotheses: [H2]\nrequires_mode: local\nworkload: {rate_rps: 10, arrival: poisson, warmup_s: 5, duration_s: 40, max_in_flight: 256, request_timeout_s: 15}\nruns: 3\nseed: 404\ndefaults:\n  resilience: {fallback: false, circuit_breaker: {enabled: false}, retries: 0}\nconditions:\n  - name: none\n    resilience: {outer_deadline_ms: 10000, timeout_ms: 10000}\n    faults: [{target: inventory-a, mode: hang, at_s: 5, duration_s: 20}]\n  - name: timeout\n    resilience: {timeout_ms: 800}\n    faults: [{target: inventory-a, mode: hang, at_s: 5, duration_s: 20}]\n  - name: timeout-retry\n    resilience: {timeout_ms: 800, retries: 2}\n    faults: [{target: inventory-a, mode: hang, at_s: 5, duration_s: 20}]\n  - name: timeout-retry-breaker\n    resilience: {timeout_ms: 800, retries: 2,\n                 circuit_breaker: {enabled: true, consecutive_failures: 5, reset_timeout_ms: 5000}}\n    faults: [{target: inventory-a, mode: hang, at_s: 5, duration_s: 20}]\n",
